{"availability":"available","full":"stir084/organic-driven-development","name":"organic-driven-development","description":"A philosophy for cultivating software as a living system that grows, adapts, heals, and evolves.","category":"Other","language":null,"stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-23T05:36:27Z","updated":"2026-06-23T06:14:19Z","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":null,"color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T05:04:48.221Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T05:04:48.221Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T05:04:48.221Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T05:04:48.221Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T05:04:48.221Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Software is not a machine to be completed. \\ It is a living system that grows, adapts, heals, and evolves.","Organic-Driven Development (ODD) is an experimental philosophy and engineering approach for cultivating software as a living system. Human groups cooperatively encode purpose, values, knowledge, and constraints; specialized agents express them through action; and the system continuously senses, remembers, repairs, and adapts.","ODD does not claim that software is biologically alive, and it is not yet a finished methodology. It uses life as a working model for discovering systems that remain healthy and coherent while their users, environment, and capabilities change."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/stir084/organic-driven-development/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a870e820ddd8f5301dfc06a9301c0fddffe85b5865d96182e479d7b45bdc2ee5","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T05:04:48.221Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T05:04:48.221Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Software is not a machine to be completed. \\ It is a living system that grows, adapts, heals, and evolves.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/stir084/organic-driven-development/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirem